      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Yes, this! \n\nI shouldn't have to take a photo from a folder in my PC, put it into another program to compress it and size it to what VRC likes, attempt an upload, figure out that it's displaying strangely or still too large, go edit it some more, and then finally get it uploaded. There should be basic tools on the website and/or in-game that compress, resize, and crop it for you. At least those tools would mean that I could put photos in my gallery and in my group's announcements MUCH easier.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
